    "receiver": "white-pack-receiver",
    "setupNotes": [
      "Factorio 2.1.24 Space Age, normal quality. Stationary in Nauvis orbit, no thrusters, no fuel, no defence (Nauvis orbit sends only small chunks). Makes 60 space science packs per minute from asteroid chunks and keeps them in the hub (stops at 2000); a cargo landing pad on Nauvis that requests packs receives them by itself. 4 asteroid collectors (one per side), 3 crushers (oxide, metallic, carbonic), 1 electric furnace, 4 assembling machine 2, 6 solar panels, 9 accumulator. Paste it anywhere on a platform made from one starter pack: it snaps to the hub. Keep the hub's \"request missing construction materials\" on: the platform then asks rockets for exactly 5000 kg (5 full rockets). Keep the wires: hub contents on red to the conditioned arms and the negating combinator; chunk values (6 each) and the crusher clock on green.",
      "Paste the blueprint anywhere on the platform: it contains the hub and snaps to the real hub. Do not use grid snapping.",
      "Keep the hub setting \"request missing construction materials\" on (the blueprint sets it). Without it the platform never asks for the parts.",
      "Rockets leave only when full (1,000 kg). The platform asks for exactly 5000 kg, which is 5 full rockets after the starter-pack rocket; any change to the bill must keep a whole number of rockets.",
      "Tick \"automatic requests from space platforms\" on the rocket silo once.",
      "Packs reach the ground through the white-pack receiver (a landing pad that requests space science packs); no click is needed after it is built."
